{"name":"Metamorphosis","hex":"#a9959f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"metamorphosis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A transformation, such as one performed by magic.","A noticeable change in character, appearance, function, or condition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metamorphosis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Metamorphosis","blocks":[{"text":"Metamorphosis is a biological process in which an animal undergoes a conspicuous and relatively abrupt change in its body structure as part of its development. Some insects, fish, amphibians, mollusks, crustaceans, cnidarians, echinoderms, and tunicates undergo metamorphosis, often accompanied by a change of nutrition or behavior. Some animal species undergo complete metamorphosis (\"holometaboly\") between radically different lifecycle stages; others have incomplete metamorphosis (\"hemimetaboly\") between somewhat similar stages, or no metamorphosis (\"ametaboly\"). Organisms with larval stages undergo metamorphosis to the adult stage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Dragonfly_metamorphosis.jpg/330px-Dragonfly_metamorphosis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metamorphosis","wikidata":"Q33753"},{"title":"Metamorphosis (Hilary Duff album)","blocks":[{"text":"Metamorphosis is the second studio album by American singer-songwriter Hilary Duff. The album was released on August 26, 2003, by Buena Vista Records and Hollywood Records as the follow-up to her Christmas album, Santa Claus Lane (2002). According to Duff, the album incorporates elements of pop and rock music, and it represents changes that are specific to her life and that everyone experiences. Duff worked with several producers on the album such as The Matrix. Others who collaborated on the album include Chico Bennett, Matthew Gerrard, John Shanks and Kara DioGuardi."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/56/Hilary_Duff_-_Metamorphosis.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metamorphosis_(Hilary_Duff_album)","wikidata":"Q1771826"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Locust_instars_NMNS.jpg/500px-Locust_instars_NMNS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Locust_instars_NMNS.jpg/1280px-Locust_instars_NMNS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Locust_instars_NMNS.jpg/500px-Locust_instars_NMNS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Incomplete metamorphosis in the grasshopper with different instar nymphs. The largest specimen is adult.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALocust_instars_NMNS.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller.jpg/250px-ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller.jpg/500px-ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller.jpg/250px-ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller2.jpg/250px-ChristianBauer_Pieris_rapae_caterpiller2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con